At Tue, 11 Apr 2006 18:21:02 +0800,
Wang, Jing J wrote:
> 
> 
> Hi, folks
> 	Is there official test suite for ALSA? In CVS, I notice there
> are testing and test directory, but seems they are all very old. So are
> they the test suite you are using for testing?

No "suite" as I know of.

For testing a normal I/O, aplay/arecord is a good one.  You can check
different I/O mode via -M and -N, and different buffer/period handling
via corresponding options, too.

For testing surrounds, speaker-test is the most suitable one.

Though, a more diagnostical tool would be helpful for debugging, too.
Any suggestions are welcome. 


